\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -China worries set safe-haven dollar for fifth straight week of gains\b0\par\par\uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2023\par 10:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON/TOKYO, Aug 18 (Reuters) - The dollar eased on Friday, but was still set for a fifth consecutive week of gains in the longest winning streak for 15 months, buoyed by demand for safer assets on worries over China's economy and bets U.S. interest rates will stay high.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set a much-stronger-than-expected daily fixing, lifting the yuan from a 9-month lows a day earlier, while sterling fell after British retail sales fell more than expected in July.\par \par \uc2 Against the yuan, the dollar edged 0.1% higher at 7.3099 in offshore trading, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the official mid-point at 7.2006, more than 1,000 pips stronger than Reuters estimate.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plumbed to a nine-month trough of 7.3490 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 China's economic troubles have deepened, with property developer China \uc2 Evergrande\uc2  seeking Chapter 15 protection in a U.S. bankruptcy court, and concerns also growing over default risks in its shadow banking sector.\par \par \uc2 Beijing has so far disappointed with stimulus, even as recent data has painted an increasingly grim picture of the economic outlook, though the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  cut rates earlier this week in a surprise move that widened the yield gap against the U.S., rendering the yuan even more vulnerable to decline.\par \par \uc2 "Developments in the distressed Chinese financial and property sector are emerging as the most prominent driver for market sentiment," said \uc2 Francesco Pesole\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ING.\par \par \uc2 "High yields and growing risks in China suggests the balance of risks is moderately tilted to the upside for the dollar," he added.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar index, which measures the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against six peers, flattened at 103.40, after touching a two-month high at 103.59 on Thursday. For the week, it is set to gain 0.5%.\par \par \uc2 Minutes from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's last meeting showed this week that most members of the rate-setting committee continued to see "significant upside risks to inflation," suggesting a bias toward further rate increases.\par \par \uc2 Strong economic data this week, particularly retail sales, had already bolstered the case for additional tightening.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the euro flattened at $1.0873, rebounding from Thursday's six-week low of $1.0856.\par \par \uc2 ING'S Pesole said the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been surprisingly resilient given the euro zone\u8217\'20\'19s economic exposure to China.\par \par \uc2 Sterling fell 0.2% against the euro to 85.46 pence after British retailers reported a bigger-than-expected drop in sales in July as heavy rain put off shoppers who are also feeling the hit from high inflation and 14 back-to-back increases in interest rates.\par \par \uc2 It touched a five-week high of 85.24 pence against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  RISK\par \par \uc2 The recent depreciation of the yen kept traders on edge against the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's authorities.\par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar eased 0.34% to 145.36 on Friday, after reaching a nine-month peak of 146.56 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In autumn of last year, the dollar's surge beyond 145 triggered the first yen buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese authorities in a generation.\par \par \uc2 However, at that time a steep drop in Treasury yields had also helped make that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  a success, which is not the case currently, \uc2 Ray Attrill\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 , wrote in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 "No such JPY tailwind this time around," he said.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar, which often trades as a proxy for China and has tended to track the yuan in recent days, gave up early gains and was flat at $0.6404, after hitting a nine-month low of $0.6365 on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the world's biggest cryptocurrency, bitcoin , slipped 0.6% to $26,488 after dipping to a fresh two-month low at $26,172, adding to a more than 7% plunge on Thursday, as a wave of risk off sentiment grips world markets.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Joice Alves in London and Kevin Buckland in Tokyo; Editing by) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-18T09:34:39.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230818ej8i00u0l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
