\par\par \b \uc2 The Japanese Yen Is Back in Uncomfortably Weak Territory -- WSJ\b0\par\par\uc2 By Frances Yoon \par \uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2023\par 12:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 When Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  approached 146 per dollar last year, its finance ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/japan-intervenes-in-currency-market-to-support-yen-11663836942"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/\b  \highlight22japan\b0 \highlight22 -\b  \highlight22intervenes\b0 \highlight22 -in-\b  \highlight22currency\b0 \highlight22 -market-to-support-yen-11663836942}}}\uc2 ) to protect the yen for the first time in decades.\par \par \uc2 It broke that level on Thursday, hitting its weakest mark against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 The yen traded as high as 146.565 per dollar during the Asian morning, before rebounding slightly in the afternoon, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The weakening came after the release of minutes from the latest \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  meeting ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/economy/central-banking/some-fed-officials-are-turning-cautious-about-raising-rates-too-high-5b998ef6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/economy/central-banking/some-fed-officials-are-turning-cautious-about-raising-rates-too-high-5b998ef6}}}\uc2 ) that raised questions about how soon the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will end its campaign of interest-rate rises. Japan's ultraloose monetary policy has put pressure on the yen, fueling its 10% decline against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 Japan's government bought yen and sold dollars last September, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was approaching 146 per dollar. \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2 , the finance minister, said at the time that the government "cannot stand by idly when speculative and excessive moves repeatedly occur."\par \par \uc2 However, Tokyo hasn't necessarily drawn a hard line in the sand around 146 per dollar. Later last year, the yen weakened past 150 ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-news-today-2022-10-20/card/yen-falls-to-22-year-low-against-dollar-RjGqe8To1D2I6e5vFHNG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-news-today-2022-10-20/card/yen-falls-to-22-year-low-against-dollar-RjGqe8To1D2I6e5vFHNG}}}\uc2 ), before staging a comeback in the last two months of the year.\par \par \uc2 NOTE: In-line links reference additional content of interest chosen by the WSJ news team.\par \par \uc2 This item is part of a Wall Street Journal live coverage event. The full stream can be found by searching P/WSJL (WSJ Live Coverage).\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 17, 2023 06:45 ET (10:45 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020230817ej8h0018v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
