\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2023\par 09:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Stocks' August Slide Continues as Treasury Yields Touch Multiyear High \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks dipped and government-bond yields reached a 15-year high after minutes from the most recent Fed policy meeting showed central bankers are worried about a possible resurgence in inflation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Demands U.S. Lift Steel, Aluminum Tariffs After WTO Ruling \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China wants the U.S. to lift tariffs imposed on its steel and aluminum products after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Trade Organization\f28 \uc2 \f2  ruled in favor of Washington against Beijing in the nations' tariff dispute. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan Exports Decline for First Time in Over Two Years \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's exports fell in July for the first time in 29 months, data from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  showed. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Rise in Australian Unemployment Strengthens Case for \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBA\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Sit Pat \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's unemployment rate rose sharply in July, adding to a growing list of data signals that suggest the peak in interest rates has been reached. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Russia's War-Torn Economy Hits Its Speed Limit \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists see this week's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gyrations not as the beginning of a financial crisis but rather as a symptom of the Kremlin's sclerotic economic prospects. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Stock Market Rally Makes More 401(k) Savers Millionaires \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The average retirement saver with a seven-figure balance is 59 years old. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Bond Yield Hits Highest Since 2008, Adding Pressure to Borrowing Costs \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on the 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  note closed at a 15-year high, threatening steeper costs for many borrowers and raising concern on Wall Street about the potential fallout in the stock, bond and housing markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Why U.S. stock-market investors need to keep an eye on a weak Japanese yen \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A weak Japanese yen is nearing levels that might prompt \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  --- an event that could send shock waves through global financial markets, analysts warn. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Some Fed Officials Are Turning Cautious about Raising Rates Too High \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials face a puzzle as inflation slows, but economic activity is firmer than anticipated. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. Importers Are Absorbing Higher Shipping Costs This Summer \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Costs to ship goods from Asia to the U.S. are turning sharply upward, but American importers appear to be absorbing the higher prices after watching freight rates plummet this year from record highs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 17, 2023 03:00 ET (07:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020230817ej8h000i2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
