\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2023\par 21:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Some Fed Officials Are Turning Cautious about Raising Rates Too High \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials face a puzzle as inflation slows, but economic activity is firmer than anticipated. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Why U.S. stock-market investors need to keep an eye on a weak Japanese yen \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A weak Japanese yen is nearing levels that might prompt \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  --- an event that could send shock waves through global financial markets, analysts warn. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Builders ramped up construction of new U.S. homes in July \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Construction on new U.S. homes rose 3.9% in July, the Commerce Department said Wednesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. Crude-Oil Inventories Fall, But Output Hits 3-Year High \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. oil inventories fell sharply last week by 6 million barrels as refiners boosted activity, but domestic crude production rose to a three-year high, government data showed. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. industrial output jumps in July on sharply higher utilities output \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. industrial production rose 1% in July, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported Wednesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China's Economic Woes are Pushing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Toward a Record Low \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Beijing wants to boost its sluggish economy and keep its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stable, but that is proving a difficult juggling act. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par New Tax-Credit Market Aims to Funnel Billions to Clean Energy \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 First deal in federal program helps fund $1.5 billion wind-energy transaction. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Mortgage demand falls as rates surge to the highest level since October 2022 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mortgage applications fell 0.8% in the latest week, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mortgage Bankers Association\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. The average rate for a 30-year mortgage is 7.16%. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Investors Need to Worry About the Bond Market's Return to Normality \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The market's best guess at the real, after-inflation, cost of money is back within the range of what once counted as normal. America has put the era of low rates behind it. Can it cope? \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.K. Inflation Slows, but Still a Worry \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The annual rate of inflation slowed but it may not be falling fast enough to convince the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  to pause interest rate increases.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 16, 2023 15:00 ET (19:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020230816ej8g002py\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
