\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits more than one-month high on China fears, yen drifts\b0\par\par\uc2 871 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2023\par 16:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  table, updates prices, adds analyst comment in\par paragraph 6 and 15)\par     By Hannah Lang and Harry  Robertson\par        WASHINGTON/LONDON, Aug 14 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar\par hit more than a one-month high on Monday as investors sought a\par safe haven due to concerns about China's economy, and traders\par braced for possible Japanese government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the\par yen hit its lowest level since November.\par     The dollar index, which tracks the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par its major peers, was up 0.36% to 103.23, its highest level in\par more than a month.\par     Analysts said investors bought the dollar as shelter from\par concerns about the health of the global economy, particularly\par China. \par     A source told Reuters that Country Garden, China's largest\par private developer, is seeking to delay payment on a private\par onshore bond for the first time, in a new sign of stress in the\par sector.\par     Meanwhile, two Chinese listed companies said at the weekend\par they had not received payment on maturing investment products\par from asset manager Zhongrong International Trust Co.\par     "A lot of traders are focusing again on China," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Edward\par Moya\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior market analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 OANDA\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "I think there's so much\par concern with just their growth outlook, with their current\par property crisis, and I think one of the biggest wealth managers\par not being able to make debt obligations is a big red\par flag."\par         Japan's yen was trading at its lowest level\par since November at 145.35 per dollar, with the dollar up 0.26%\par against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The Bank of Japan has stuck to its ultra-loose monetary\par policy as other global central banks hiked interest rates,\par making returns in other countries look more attractive and\par weighing heavily on the yen.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets last September when the\par dollar rose past 145 yen, prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par (MOF) to buy the yen and push the pair back to around 140 yen.\par The yen is down nearly 10% against the dollar for the year.\par     "Lack of verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far suggests that the\par patience level of Japanese authorities may have gone up after\par the latest tweak to monetary policy and the disinflation trends\par in the United States," said Charu Chanana, a market strategist\par at Saxo Markets. \par     "Still, traders are potentially cautious of that 145\par handle."\par     The Australian dollar slid to its lowest level\par since May at $0.6456 and was last down 0.30% versus the U.S.\par dollar at $0.648. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is often seen as a proxy for\par investor sentiment on China.\par     Sterling was last down 0.34% to $1.2653, while the\par euro was 0.46% lower at $1.08965.\par     Russia's rouble fell past 100 per U.S. dollar\par on Monday, driven in large part by the Russian current account\par surplus shrinking as energy export revenue dropped and\par government spending on the Ukraine war remained high.\par     "Whenever you fall through some key technical levels, it\par reminds traders, it reminds markets of just how hard hitting\par this war has been on the Russian economy," said Moya.\par     Economic data could move \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later in the week, as\par investors will scrutinize Chinese industrial output and consumer\par spending data on Tuesday, before minutes from the latest \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S.\par Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  meeting on Wednesday. British inflation figures\par are also due on Wednesday.\par     Japanese GDP data is due on Tuesday, ahead of inflation\par figures on Friday.\par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:30AM (1430 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 103.2300       102.8700    +0.36%         -0.251%       +103.4600   +102.7600\par  Euro/Dollar                  $1.0896        $1.0947     -0.46%         +1.69%        +$1.0965    +$1.0874\par  Dollar/Yen                   145.3150       144.9550    +0.26%         +10.85%       +145.5700   +144.6500\par  Euro/Yen                     158.35         158.65      -0.19%         +12.87%       +158.8200   +158.2000\par  Dollar/Swiss                 0.8794         0.8764      +0.37%         -4.87%        +0.8828     +0.8756\par  Sterling/Dollar              $1.2654        $1.2697     -0.34%         +4.63%        +$1.2713    +$1.2617\par  Dollar/Canadian              1.3460         1.3446      +0.12%         -0.64%        +1.3478     +1.3437\par  Aussie/Dollar                $0.6476        $0.6498     -0.30%         -4.97%        +$0.6503    +$0.6454\par  Euro/Swiss                   0.9582         0.