\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar steady after CPI data bolsters Fed pause bets; yen nears 145\b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2023\par 03:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 11 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady on Friday as traders wagered that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  is done with rate hikes after data showed U.S. consumer prices increased moderately in July, while the yen was flirting with the psychologically key 145 level.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen eased 0.10% to 144.89 per dollar in early Asian hours, its lowest since June 30, when it also briefly breached 145 per dollar level, stoking investor fears of another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Japanese authorities.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September last year when the dollar rose past 145 yen, pushing the pair to around 140 yen as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought the yen to weaken the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The yen was also lower against the euro at 159.135, just shy of the 15-year peak of 159.19 it touched on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Saxo Markets strategists said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears might lead to some profit taking, but noted that the Japanese authorities are likely to continue to be patient.\par \par \uc2 With Japan on holiday on Friday, liquidity is expected to be thin.\par \par \uc2 Overnight, data showed the U.S. consumer price index rose 0.2% last month, matching the gain in June, with the CPI climbing 3.2% in the 12 months through July.\par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters had forecast the CPI would rise 0.2% last month and by 3.3% on a year-on-year basis.\par \par \uc2 Moderating inflation, together with an easing labour market, has bolstered economists' conviction that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be able to engineer a "soft landing" for the economy.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation is grinding back towards target and the labour market is slowly cooling," said Ryan Brandham, head of global capital markets for North America at Validus Risk Management.\par \par \uc2 "But the FOMC will want to see yet more data before deciding in September if progress has been fast enough to warrant a pause, or if the balance of risks calls for another hike to ensure inflation targets are met."\par \par \uc2 Traders of futures tied to the Fed's policy rate see less than a 10% chance that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase its benchmark overnight interest rate from its current 5.25%-5.50% range at a Sept. 19-20 policy meeting. The Fed's first rate cut is priced into the futures contracts by March of 2024.\par \par \uc2 "Market pricing currently favours a pause, but the market has underpriced the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s actions before," Brandham cautioned.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which measures the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against six rivals, eased 0.078% to 102.54, but was on course to clock gains for the fourth straight week.\par \par \uc2 The euro was up 0.08% to $1.0988, while the kiwi eased 0.03% to $0.602.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar rose 0.20% to $0.6534. Earlier, the head of \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was possible some further tightening will be required, but appeared to suggest the amount of rate hikes so far should be sufficient to bring inflation to heel.\par \par \uc2 Appearing before lawmakers, outgoing \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  Governor \uc2 Philip Lowe\uc2  said the recent data so far are consistent with the economy continuing to travel along the "narrow path" to a soft landing.\par \par \uc2 Sterling was last at $1.2684, up 0.07% on the day, looking to snap its three-day losing streak ahead of GDP data.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ankur Banerjee in Singapore Editing by Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-11T02:57:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230811ej8b005h9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
