\par\par \b \uc2 Japanese bonds see biggest weekly foreign outflow since mid-Jan\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2023\par 09:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Aug 10 (Reuters) - Foreign investors withdrew sharply from Japanese bonds last week, as the local bonds yields continued to rise after the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  tweaked its yield control policy.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners offloaded a net 1.97 trillion yen ($13.70 billion) worth of Japanese bonds with maturity of over an year in the week ended Aug. 5, the biggest amount since Jan. 13, data from \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, short-term Japanese debt securities received about 768.6 billion yen worth of foreign capital.\par \par \uc2 "Foreign outflows are likely driven by worries of a sell-off in JGBs after \uc2 BOJ\uc2  relaxed its Yield Curve Control policy on 28 July," said Wei-Liang Chang, a \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Credit Strategist \uc2 DBS Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Further outflows could materialize if inflation drifts higher in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which may spur speculation of reduced \uc2 BOJ\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth yields."\par \par \uc2 Yield on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 10-year government bond, which move inversely to prices, rose to a 9-1/2-year high of 0.655% last week.\par \par \uc2 According to data from Japanese exchanges, foreigners withdrew about 386.6 billion yen from domestic equities during the week as they remained net sellers for a second consecutive week.\par \par \uc2 They sold about 405.05 billion yen worth of derivatives on a net basis but purchased cash equities worth 18.85 billion yen, remaining net buyers for the sixth straight week.\par \par \uc2 Japanese stocks have drawn about 7.91 trillion yen worth of foreign investments so far this year on a net basis, compared with about 1.32 trillion yen in outflows last year.\par \par \uc2 Japanese investors secured about 488.8 billion yen worth of long-term and 127 billion yen worth of short-term overseas bonds, marking their biggest weekly net purchase in five weeks.\par \par \uc2 They, however, withdrew 352.2 billion yen from foreign equities in a sixth successive week of net selling. ($1 = 143.8200 yen)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Gaurav Dogra and Patturaja Murugaboopathy in Bengaluru; Editing by Rashmi Aich) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-10T08:58:25.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230810ej8a0139y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
