n.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In recent months, the exchange rate for the U.S. dollar against the yen has sharply increased. As of July 31, 2023, the spot buying rate quoted on the Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as reported by the BOJ at 5:00 p.m., Tokyo time, was \u165\'00\'A5142.17 = $1.00, and the noon buying rate on July 28, 2023 for cable transfers in New York City payable in yen, as reported by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York, was \u165\'00\'A5140.72 = $1.00.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is conducted to influence \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates by buying and selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. In \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is to be carried out under the authority of the Minister of Finance. The BOJ conducts \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on behalf of and at the instruction of the minister. When the minister deems it necessary to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gives the BOJ specific instructions for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . With respect to funding, as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  involves buying and selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it requires funds such as Japanese yen and U.S. dollars. In Japan, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Fund Special Account (FEFSA), which falls under the jurisdiction of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is used for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The total amount of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the MOF for the period from August 30, 2022 through October 27, 2022 was \u165\'00\'A59,188.1 billion. Following such \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Japan's reserve assets totaled $1,194,568 million as of October 31, 2022, down $97,504 million from the end of August. As of June 30, 2023, Japan's reserve assets totaled $1,247,179 million.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign Direct Investment\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table sets forth information regarding annual foreign direct investment in Japan and annual foreign direct investment abroad for the periods indicated.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign direct investment in Japan (by industry)(a)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                  2018                               2019                 2020         2021          2022   \par                                                                                                                            \par                                  (in billions of yen)   \par Manufacturing (total)(b)         \u165\'00\'A5                      1,188.5            \u165\'00\'A5   606.7              \u165\'00\'A5   258.2         \u165\'00\'A5      1,800.8       \u165\'00\'A5   1,644.1   \par Food                                                    9.8                    58.2                   -43.9                28.3              3.4       \par Textile                                                 -4.2                   2.7                    4.2                  6.5               11.5      \