\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan asks X to take down fake account of top  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  diplomat as yen weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2023\par 09:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Update Aug 3 story with suspension of account in paragraph 3 and description of Kanda's comment in paragraph 8)\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 3 (Reuters) - \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) warned on Thursday of a fake account for its top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Masato Kanda on social media X, formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , as the market fears a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid the yen's drop to a one-month-low.\par \par \uc2 In a rare English-language post on X, the ministry said "Please don't follow the impersonation account and/or comment on the post", saying such an X account purportedly belonging to Kanda or his staff did not exist.\par \par \uc2 "MOF is currently requesting that X (formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ) suspends the impersonation account. Thank you for your cooperation" it said, in its official account {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MOF_Japan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . The social media platform suspended the fake account within hours.\par \par \uc2 The account, under the name "Masato Kanda" and the user ID "@Jgghkj_", appeared to have been created in March and made only five posts to date, including three pictures of Kanda posted on March 1. The latest post, made at 3:56 pm (0656 GMT), appeared to have impersonated Kanda's recent trip to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Kanda was in Ukraine on Wednesday to explain Japan's support for the country, the MOF had announced.\par \par \uc2 The fake account, which was following about 5,000 users and was followed by little more than 550, had made no remarks about the yen or financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Kanda, Japan's vice-minister of finance for international affairs, has been the central figure in the country's efforts to stem the sharp decline of its yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since last year, supervising record yen-buying, dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last year.\par \par \uc2 Prior to the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's latest July 27-28 policy meeting, Kanda, in an unusual move, referred to market speculation about a possible tweak to monetary policy, in addition to warning the market that authorities will consider all options to deal with the yen's excess volatility.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  surprised markets with a tweak to its bond yield control programme last week, allowing interest rates to rise more freely.\par \par \uc2 The yen weakened on Thursday to hit 143.89 against U.S. dollar, its lowest since July 7, as \uc2 BOJ\uc2  announced emergency bond purchases to check a surge in 10-year bond yields.\par \par \uc2 Markets are closely watching the MOF's next moves as the yen is nearing 145 per dollar again, a level that triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998 last September. (Reporting by Kantaro Komiya; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-8-4T08:27:07.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230804ej8400uv5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
