\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-BOJ won't tweak YCC in July, say 77% of economists\b0\par\par\uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2023\par 06:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/econ-polls?RIC=JPGDPQP GDP poll data\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/econ-polls?RIC=JPCPIQP core CPI poll data\par \par \uc2 By Satoshi Sugiyama\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 21 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will hold steady its policy including its yield control scheme at next week's meeting, more than three-quarters of economists polled by Reuters said, as policymakers stress more time is needed for inflation stability.\par \par \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Kazuo Ueda\uc2  has signalled his resolve to maintain its massive monetary stimulus, despite inflation persistently outpacing the bank's 2% target.\par \par \uc2 Only five of 22 economists, or 23%, expect the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  to start scaling back its ultra-loose easing and tweak yield curve control (YCC) at this month's monetary policy review, the July 10-19 survey found, down from 43% in a June poll.\par \par \uc2 Just half of those respondents, 11 of 22, anticipate a rollback of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's easing policy by year-end.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  may start the phase-out in October at the earliest when they release the quarterly price outlook, or in December depending on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and yield rate situations," said Mari Iwashita, chief market economist at \uc2 Daiwa Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It could also be in January next year if they wait to have a glimpse at next year's spring wage negotiations," she said.\par \par \uc2 A separate question on when the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  will end YCC showed a wide range of views. Three of 22 economists said later this year, five chose the first half of next year, six opted for the latter half of next year and eight said for "2025 or later".\par \par \uc2 If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to tweak YCC before ending it, 10 economists said it would widen the 10-year yield fluctuation range from the current 0.5% band, while nine said it would change the control target to a shorter yield.\par \par \uc2 With interest rate differential between Japan and the United States not expected to widen any further, the yen strengthened close to 5% from seven-month-low 145 per dollar hit in late June. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded around 140 per dollar on Friday morning.\par \par \uc2 Asked about at what yen level the Japanese government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline, 14 of 21 economists, or two-thirds, said 150 per dollar. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in October.\par \par \uc2 WAGE GROWTH\par \par \uc2 Japanese companies offered their biggest pay hike in three decades this year to compensate workers for the rising cost of living. \uc2 BOJ\uc2  officials regard sustained wage growth as an essential condition for an exit from ultra-loose policy.\par \par \uc2 Analysts polled were evenly split on a question asking whether next year's wage growth would be strong enough for the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  to consider monetary policy normalisation.\par \par \uc2 Twelve of 24 said it was likely, including one saying "very likely", whereas the other 12 that would be unlikely.\par \par \uc2 Hiroshi Namioka, chief strategist at T&D Asset Management, said corporate managers need to rethink their approach to wage growth.\par \par \uc2 "This year, it was 'prices are going up, and other companies around us seem to be raising wages, so let's raise ours, too,'" he said. "This must be changed to 'raise wages to secure good talent.'"\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the Reuters global long-term economic outlook polls package:) (Reporting by Satoshi Sugiyama; Additional reporting by Kantaro Komiya; Polling by Milounee Purohit and Anant Chandak; Editing by Sam Holmes)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-24T04:05:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230721ej7l00ckw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
