\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen firms amid  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  chatter, Aussie rises on \uc2 RBA\uc2  decision\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2023\par 11:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices at 0833 GMT, adds analyst comment from paragraph 10)\par \par \uc2 By Ankur Banerjee and Harry Robertson\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE/LONDON, July 4 (Reuters) - The dollar fell slightly against the yen on Tuesday as markets remained on high alert for signs of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the Australian dollar gained after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held interest rates steady.\par \par \uc2 The greenback was down 0.19% by 0833 GMT to 144.45 yen , after rising 0.27% on Monday.\par \par \uc2 However, the yen remained close to last week's almost eight-month low of 145.07 per dollar, which prompted Japan's Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  to warn against excessive yen selling.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  (\uc2 RBA\uc2 ) held interest rates steady at 4.10% on Tuesday, saying it wanted more time to assess the impact of past hikes, but warned further tightening might be needed to bring inflation to heel.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar bounced around, but was up 0.13% at 0833 GMT to $0.668.\par \par \uc2 Markets had leant towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holding rates steady after inflation eased a little more than expected in May. Economists however were split, with 16 out of 31 polled by Reuters expecting a hike and the rest forecasting the bank would maintain current rates.\par \par \uc2 Market activity was relatively subdued on Tuesday with U.S. trade closed for the July 4 public holiday. Investors were also waiting for the closely watched U.S. non-farm payrolls employment report due on Friday, which is likely to influence the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's next decision.\par \par \uc2 The euro was down 0.13% against the dollar at $1.09, while sterling was roughly flat at $1.269.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar index, which tracks the greenback against six major peers, was also little changed at 103.\par \par \uc2 "It feels like every week will bring something and this week we're waiting for the U.S. non-farm payrolls," said \uc2 Alvin Tan\uc2 , head of Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Across \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, investors also remained on watch for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities to stem yen losses.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Tuesday, Japan's top financial diplomat Masato Kanda said that officials were in close contact with \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  and other overseas authorities almost everyday on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and broader financial markets.\par \par \uc2 "This is sending signals that a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be coming as yen continues to hover above 144 per dollar," said Charu Chanana, market strategist at Saxo Markets.\par \par \uc2 "A coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually has a longer lasting impact on the yen than a unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought yen in September, its first foray into the market to boost its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998, as the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's pledge to retain ultra-loose policy as long as required drove the yen as low as 145 per dollar. It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in October after the yen plunged to a 32-year low of 151.94.\par \par \uc2 RBC\uc2 's Tan said he thinks the dollar is likely to rise past 150 yen.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is still unwilling yet to move away from the YCC policy, that's going to result in a higher dollar," he said, referring to Japan's yield curve control that keeps bond market rates low.\par \par \uc2 Tan said such a move would make \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "more likely than not".\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ankur Banerjee in Singapore and Harry Robertson in London, additional reporting by Kevin Buckland Editing by Shri Navaratnam and Emma Rumney) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-4T10:01:55.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230704ej740141u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
