\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen weakens on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  threat; slowdown fears weigh on euro\b0\par\par\uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2023\par 14:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON, July 3 (Reuters) - The yen fell on Monday to near eight-month lows against the dollar as investors said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in sight, while the euro weakened after a slowdown in factory activity in China and the euro zone renewed economic growth fears.\par \par \uc2 The dollar edged up ahead of the July 4 holiday after U.S. economic data last week showed slightly easing inflation and consumer spending.\par \par \uc2 The yen weakened 0.37% to 144.86, after it touched its lowest level against the greenback since November on Friday. It lost 9% against the dollar in the first six months of the year as investors kept a close eye on whether Japanese authorities would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  on Friday said Japan would take appropriate steps in response to excessive yen weakening, the latest of a series of comments from government ministers and officials.\par \par \uc2 "The yen is on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch, and the next data focus is \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's May wage growth due 7 July," said Paul Mackel, Global Head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Research at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japan bought yen in September, its first foray in the market to boost its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998, after a \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) decision to maintain ultra-loose policy drove the yen as low as 145 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in October after the yen plunged to a 32-year low of 151.94. Still, Japanese business sentiment improved in the second quarter as easing supply constraints and the removal of pandemic curbs lifted factory output and consumption.\par \par \uc2 FEARS FROM CHINA\par \par \uc2 Fears of a slowdown in the global economy have weighed on the euro, which started the third quarter down 0.1% at $1.0897, after rising for three consecutive quarters. A private sector survey showed on Monday that China's factory activity growth slowed in June, with sentiment waning and recruitment cooling as firms grew increasingly concerned about sluggish market conditions.\par \par \uc2 Euro zone manufacturing activity contracted faster than initially thought in June as persistent policy tightening by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  squeezed finances, a survey showed on Monday, painting an increasingly gloomy outlook for industry.\par \par \uc2 "Investors have commented that the euro zone cyclical story is losing momentum, and this is why the euro should be lower," \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's Mackel said adding that the euro is, however, holding up relatively well.\par \par \uc2 China's onshore yuan steadied at 7.2494 after slipping to near eight-month lows against the dollar at the end of last week, supported by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intensified efforts to stabilise the much weakened local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WEEK AHEAD Investor focus this week will be on the minutes of the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's June meeting due on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to leave interest rates unchanged in its June meeting but hinted that borrowing costs may still need to rise by as much as half of a percentage point by the end of the year. Economic data eased recession worries. Data on Friday showed cooler-than-expected inflation in May, while consumer spending abruptly decelerated.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. economy is not slowing as forecast," \uc2 Citi\uc2  strategists said in a client note. "Surprisingly strong job growth is keeping labour markets tight while providing the nominal spending power to drive services consumption." Markets are pricing in a 90% chance of the Fed hiking rates by 25 basis points in its July meeting, CME FedWatch tool showed.\par \par \uc2 Investor attention will also be on the Labor Department's Job Openings and Labor Turnover Survey, or JOLTS, and monthly payrolls report due later this week that will help gauge the labour market in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar rose 0.16% to 103.11, after eking out a near 2% gain in the first half of the year.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Joice Alves in London, additional reporting by Ankur Banerjee in Singapore; Editing by David Evans and Conor Humprhies) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-3T13:19:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230703ej7301sfi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
