\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen weak, dollar drifts as traders weigh Fed rate hike path\b0\par\par\uc2 732 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2023\par 07:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, July 3 (Reuters) - The yen remained hunkered just below the psychologically important barrier of 145 per U.S. dollar on Monday, while the dollar was on the back foot after U.S. economic data last week showed slightly easing inflation and consumer spending.\par \par \uc2 The yen weakened 0.09% to 144.45 to start the second half of the year, having lost 9% against the dollar in the first six months of the year.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the yen was hovering at 157.66, just under the 15-year low of 158 it touched last week. It rose to 183.58 per sterling, its highest since December 2015.\par \par \uc2 The Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly passed 145 per dollar on Friday, hitting a near eight-month low of 145.07 as investors keep an eye on whether Japanese authorities will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said on Friday Japan would take appropriate steps in response to excessive yen weakening, in the latest comment from government ministers and officials.\par \par \uc2 The comments from Suzuki helped curb the yen's losses on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is best conceived of as an escalation ladder," said \uc2 Marc Chandler\uc2 , chief market strategist at Bannockburn \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Among the highest rungs is the coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... The low rungs on the escalation ladder are different types of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought yen in September, its first foray in the market to boost its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998, after a \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) decision to maintain ultra-loose policy drove the yen as low as 145 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in October after the yen plunged to a 32-year low of 151.94.\par \par \uc2 Still, Japanese business sentiment improved in the second quarter as easing supply constraints and the removal of pandemic curbs lifted factory output and consumption, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  survey showed, a sign the economy was on course for a steady recovery.\par \par \uc2 Investor focus this week will be on the minutes of the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's June meeting due on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to leave interest rates unchanged in its June meeting but hinted that borrowing costs may still need to rise by as much as half of a percentage point by the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 Economic data through last week painted a picture of resilient U.S. economy that eased recession worries but stoked expectations that the Fed will stick to its hawkish path.\par \par \uc2 But data on Friday showed cooler-than-expected inflation in May, while consumer spending abruptly decelerated, providing further evidence that the Fed's hikes are having their desired effect.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. economy is not slowing as forecast," \uc2 Citi\uc2  strategists said in a client note. "Surprisingly strong job growth is keeping labour markets tight while providing the nominal spending power to drive services consumption."\par \par \uc2 Markets are pricing in a 84% chance of the Fed hiking rates by 25 basis points in its July meeting, CME FedWatch tool showed.\par \par \uc2 Investor attention will also be on the Labor Department's Job Openings and Labor Turnover Survey, or JOLTS, and monthly payrolls report due later this week that will help gauge the labour market in the United States.\par \par \uc2 NatWest Markets\uc2  strategists expect the hiking cycle to be over, but noted that the lack of sufficient-enough progress in the inflation data could lead officials to hike by 25 bps again in July.\par \par \uc2 "The decision to act or not will be more data dependent than ever," they said.\par \par \uc2 Against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar was at 102.86, having dropped 0.4% on Friday. After eking out a near 2% gain in the first half of the year, the euro made subdued start to the third quarter and was at $1.0916, up 0.05%.\par \par \uc2 Sterling last fetched $1.2704, flat on the day, after rising 5% in the first six months of the year.\par \par \uc2 China's yuan steadied after slipping to near eight-month lows against the dollar at the end of last week, supported by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intensified efforts to stabilise the much weakened local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar rose 0.02% to $0.667, while the New Zealand dollar rose 0.42% at $0.615.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Ankur Banerjee in Singapore; Editing by Christopher Cushing and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-7-3T06:26:29.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230703ej7300jah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
