\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen tentative, dollar soft as traders weigh Fed rate hike path\b0\par\par\uc2 840 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2023\par 04:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ankur Banerjee\par        SINGAPORE, July 3 (Reuters) - The yen remained hunkered\par just below the psychologically important barrier of 145 per U.S.\par dollar on Monday, while the dollar was on the back foot after\par U.S. economic data last week showed slightly easing inflation\par and consumer spending. \par     The yen weakened 0.03% to 144.38 per dollar in\par early Asian hours to kick start the second half of the year\par having dropped 9% against the dollar in the first six months of\par the year. \par     Against the euro, the yen was hovering at\par 157.495, below the 15-year low of 158 it touched last week. It\par was at 183.47 per sterling, just below the\par seven-and-a-half-year low of 183.86 it hit on Friday.\par     The Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  briefly passed 145 per dollar on Friday,\par hitting a near eight-month low of 145.07 as investors keep an\par eye on whether Japanese authorities will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shunichi Suzuki\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Friday said Japan would\par take appropriate steps in response to excessive yen weakening,\par in the latest comment from government ministers and officials.\par     "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is best conceived of as an escalation ladder,"\par  said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marc Chandler\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief market strategist at Bannockburn\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     "Among the highest rungs is the coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ...\par The low rungs on the escalation ladder are different types of\par verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought yen in September, its first foray in the market\par to boost its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since 1998, after a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\par decision to maintain ultra-loose policy drove the yen as low as\par 145 per dollar. \par     It \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in October after the yen plunged to a\par 32-year low of 151.94.\par     Still, business sentiment improved in the second quarter as\par easing supply constraints and the removal of pandemic curbs\par lifted factory output and consumption, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  survey\par showed, a sign the economy was on course for a steady recovery.\par     Investor focus this week will be on the minutes of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S.\par Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's June meeting due on Wednesday. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decided to leave interest rates unchanged\par in its June meeting but hinted that borrowing costs may still\par need to rise by as much as half of a percentage point by the end\par of the year.\par     Data on Friday showed cooler-than-expected inflation in May,\par while consumer spending abruptly decelerated, providing further\par evidence that the Fed's hikes are having their desired effect.\par     The personal consumption expenditures (PCE) price index\par gained 0.1% for the month after a 0.4% rise in April. It\par advanced 3.8% on an annual basis, slowing from a revised 4.3%\par the prior month.\par     The PCE gauges were still well above the Fed's 2% inflation\par target.\par     "The U.S. economy is not slowing as forecast," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citi\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par strategists said in a client note. "Surprisingly strong job\par growth is keeping labour markets tight while providing the\par nominal spending power to drive services consumption."\par     Markets are pricing in a 84% chance of the Fed hiking rates\par by 25 basis points in its July meeting, CME FedWatch tool\par showed.\par     Investor attention will also be on the Labor Department's\par Job Openings and Labor Turnover Survey, or JOLTS and monthly\par payrolls report due later this week that will help gauge the\par labour market in the United States. \par     Against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the dollar was at\par 102.94, having dropped 0.4% on Friday. The euro eased\par 0.04% to $1.0906. Sterling last fetched $1.2694, down\par 0.08% on the day.\par    In cryptocurrencies, bitcoin last rose 1.02% to\par $30,699.00. Ethereum last rose 0.88% to\par $1,943.94.\par     The Australian dollar fell 0.14% to $0.666, while\par the New Zealand dollar rose 0.16% to $0.613.\par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0142 GMT\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct     High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                 \par                                               Session                                           \par  Euro/Dollar                  $1.0915        $1.0909     +0.06%         +1.87%      +1.0917     +1.0901\par  Dollar/Yen                   144.4450       144.3350    +0.10%         +10.10%     +144.5300   +144.4650\par  Euro/Yen         <EURJPY=EB  157.67         157.44      +0.15%         +12.38%     +157.6800   +157.3200\par                   S>   