\par\par \b \uc2 Yen May Weaken Further as Interest Rates Diverge -- Talking Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ronnie Harui \par \uc2 634 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juni 2023\par 06:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The yen may weaken more in coming months on expectations that the interest-rate gap between Japan and most other countries could widen further and hurt the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts say.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  Governor \uc2 Kazuo Ueda\uc2  said Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't yet confident enough to alter its super-accommodative monetary policy and argued that Japan's underlying inflation is still below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 2%. On the same day, Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  said that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep raising rates despite leaving rates unchanged earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 "The combination of sticky U.S. inflation, which keeps the Fed from reversing rate hikes, and a patient \uc2 BOJ\uc2 , which limits the extent of policy normalization, could prolong the yen weakness," said Shusuke Yamada, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /Rates strategist at Bank of America Securities Japan, in a recent research report. BofA Securities Japan also raised its third- and fourth-quarter dollar-yen forecasts to 147.00 from 143.00 and to 145.00 from 140.00, respectively.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was recently at 144.52 yen after touching JPY144.63 on Wednesday, its highest intraday level since November 2022. The yen is on course to weaken 8.1% against the dollar this quarter, the largest quarterly depreciation since April-June 2022, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  at its June 16 policy decision left short-term interest rates at minus 0.1% and maintained the cap on the 10-year Japanese government bond yield at 0.5%. On the other side of the Pacific, Fed officials this month kept the benchmark federal-funds rate in a 5.00%-5.25% range after raising it rapidly over 10 straight meetings. Another increase at the Fed's July 25-26 meeting would bring the policy rate to a 22-year high.\par \par \uc2 The difference in policy rates weakens the yen as investors typically sell a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that gets low interest rates and use the proceeds for investments in assets denominated in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have high interest rates.\par \par \uc2 "The key fundamental driver of yen weakness is the policy divergence between the Fed and the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 , which appears in no hurry to shift away from its yield-curve-control policy yet," says \uc2 Alvin T. Tan\uc2 , head of Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategy at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 , in an email.\par \par \uc2 To be sure, some analysts think the yen could strengthen given the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities or possible adjustments to the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's yield-curve-control policy.\par \par \uc2 Just Tuesday, Japan's Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  highlighted his view that yen-dollar exchange rate movements are "one-sided and rapid."\par \par \uc2 Asked whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was considering yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, a strategy it used last fall, Suzuki replied that the government would "take the appropriate response" in the case of excessive movements.\par \par \uc2 The speed and extent of the yen's weakness are limited by the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which last happened when dollar-yen was in the 145-152 range, said \uc2 Barclays\uc2 ' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists Shinichiro Kadota and Lhamsuren Sharavdemberel in a recent research report.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2  also expects a one-off 3%-5% appreciation of the yen that could result from a possible change or an abandonment of the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's YCC policy. But the impact on the yen might be contained, partly owing to possible dip-buying demand in dollar-yen, the strategists added. The U.K. bank forecasts dollar-yen at 137.00 in the third quarter and 135.00 in the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ronnie Harui at ronnie.harui@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 29, 2023 00:41 ET (04:41 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020230629ej6t0007i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
