\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Asia shares subdued, yen shunned as euro shines\b0\par\par\uc2 812 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2023\par 07:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asian stock markets : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2zpUAr4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Yen near 15-yr low on rising euro, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  a risk\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Upbeat US data, hawkish \uc2 ECB\uc2  fuels rate speculation\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tech stocks hit by report US to limit AI chips for China\par \par \uc2 By Wayne Cole\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, June 28 (Reuters) - Asian shares stalled on Wednesday as surprisingly upbeat U.S. economic news warred with global growth concerns, while the embattled yen hit a 15-year low on the euro and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hinted at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent further losses.\par \par \uc2 The strength of U.S. data also combined with hawkish commentary from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to undermine bonds as markets narrowed the odds on further rate hikes.\par \par \uc2 That only heightened attention on a star-studded panel of central bankers later in the day in Portugal which includes Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , \uc2 ECB\uc2  head \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  Governor Kazuo Ueda.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. data signals continued resilience in interest rate sensitive sectors, and the Fed is very clear that a period of sub-trend activity may be needed to bring inflation under control," said analysts at ANZ. "So far, that doesn't seem to be happening."\par \par \uc2 "For the \uc2 ECB\uc2 , senior officials signalled the need for ongoing tightening unless core inflation slows materially and a September rate hike is looking increasingly on the cards."\par \par \uc2 The rate risk kept markets cautious and MSCI's broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan was off 0.2%.\par \par \uc2 Chinese blue chips dipped 0.6% and the yuan eased anew after Beijing fixed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower than many had expected, sowing confusion about whether policy makers really wanted to slow its slide.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment was not helped by a Wall Street Journal report that Washington was considering new restrictions on exports of artificial intelligence chips to China.\par \par \uc2 The report knocked \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  3% lower after the bell and dragged Nasdaq futures down 0.4%.\par \par \uc2 Yet it seemed to be welcome news for Japan's tech companies, which drove a 1.5% rally in the Nikkei. Chip groups \uc2 Tokyo Electron\uc2  and \uc2 Advantest\uc2  led the gains.\par \par \uc2 EUROSTOXX 50 futures added 0.3% and FTSE futures 0.2%.\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 futures dipped 0.2%, though that followed solid gains on Tuesday as U.S. data on housing, durable goods orders and consumer sentiment handily topped expectations.\par \par \uc2 "The data indicated a firmer pace of residential, inventory, and equipment investment in the second quarter," wrote analysts at \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 . "We boosted our Q2 GDP tracking estimate by 0.4pp to +2.2%."\par \par \uc2 That resilience offset recent softness in manufacturing surveys and led the market to narrow the odds on a July rate hike from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Futures now imply around a 77% chance of a hike to 5.25-5.5%, and slightly more risk of a further move to 5.5-5.75%, which nudged short-term Treasury yields higher.\par \par \uc2 EURO ON THE RISE\par \par \uc2 Bond yields also moved sharply higher in Europe after a bevy of central bankers sounded hawkish on inflation and warned rates would likely have to stay higher for longer.\par \par \uc2 Markets imply a 90% probability of an \uc2 ECB\uc2  rate hike to 3.75% in July and a peak around 4.0%.\par \par \uc2 That underpinned the euro at $1.0950, while keeping it near a 15-year peak of 157.97 yen.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had hit a near eight-month top of 144.18 yen , before easing back to 143.96 as Japanese officials again protested against the yen's weakness.\par \par \uc2 Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Masato Kanda on Wednesday warned against further falls in the yen, saying authorities would take an appropriate response if moves became excessive.\par \par \uc2 Markets are wary in case \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the yen as it did last October, which knocked the dollar down from a top of 151.94 to as low as 144.50 in a matter of hours.\par \par \uc2 Yet, a rally in the yen looks unlikely while the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  maintains its super-easy monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 "Following \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor Ueda's consistently dovish message and weak Japanese wage growth, market participants now lack the conviction the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  will soon tighten its monetary policy," said Carol Kong, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 CBA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "So we now see a higher risk Japanese authorities will step into the market to prop up the JPY."\par \par \uc2 In commodities, gold steadied at $1,915 an ounce, after finding support at the recent three-month low of $1,909.99.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices edged up after data showed a larger-than-expected draw in U.S. crude and gasoline inventories, but remains uncomfortably close to its lows for the year so far.\par \par \uc2 Brent firmed 33 cents to $72.59 a barrel, while U.S. crude rose 20 cents to $67.90.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Lincoln Feast and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-28T06:29:35.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230628ej6s00hqx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
