\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen under pressure; Aussie slides as inflation slows\b0\par\par\uc2 905 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2023\par 07:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ankur Banerjee\par        SINGAPORE, June 28 (Reuters) - The yen struggled against\par most major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday, hovering near a 15-year low\par against the euro as Japanese authorities did not rule out\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem losses, while the Australian dollar dived\par lower as inflation eased in May.\par     Japanese authorities are under renewed pressure to combat\par the yen's fresh declines driven by market expectations that the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  will keep interest rates ultra-low, even as other\par central banks tighten monetary policy to curb inflation.\par      "We are closely watching \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves with a strong sense\par of urgency," Japan's top \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  diplomat Masato Kanda told\par reporters on Wednesday. \par     "We will respond appropriately if it becomes excessive."\par     The yen was hovering around the seven-month low of\par 144.18 per dollar it touched overnight. It was last at 144. \par     Against the euro, the yen was pinned near the\par 15-year low of 157.93 it hit on Tuesday. Against sterling, the\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was hovering around 183.25, just a\par shade below the 7.5-year low it touched on Tuesday.\par     "With the rise in the dollar against the yen set to run\par further, we judge the risk has increased the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by buying the JPY," said Carol Kong,\par a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2 .  \par     "However, we note it is the speed of change, rather than the\par level, that matters most in the (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Japanese finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2 's)\par decision to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Kong said.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made forays into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to prop up the\par yen last September and October to stem a plunge in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par which hit a 32-year low of 151.94 to the dollar.\par     While the yen is still well off that trough, many market\par players see 145 as Tokyo's line in the sand, which if breached\par could trigger another round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     \par     Meanwhile, the Australian dollar skidded to a\par three-week low of $0.6618 after the local consumer price\par inflation rate slowed to a 13-month low in May. \par     The Aussie was last down 0.64% at $0.66435. The kiwi\par  fell 0.71% to $0.612\par     A measure of core inflation also cooled, in a sign interest\par rates might not have to rise again in July.\par     The yuan steadied against the dollar on Wednesday, a day\par after China's monetary authorities took forceful action to\par support the sliding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for the first time in nearly eight\par months.\par     The offshore yuan was at $7.2348 per dollar. In the\par spot market, the onshore yuan opened at 7.2225 per\par dollar and was changing hands at 7.2285.        \par     Overnight, data showed that U.S. consumer confidence\par increased in June to the highest level in nearly 1.5 years,\par while business spending appeared to hold up in May, indicating\par the economy remained on solid footing. \par     The latest slew of data reinforced views of a resilient U.S.\par economy and eased worries of a recession, though it also\par indicated that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may have to continue raising\par rates.\par     Markets are pricing in a 77% probability of a 25 basis point\par hike by the Fed next month, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME\f28 \uc2 \f2  FedWatch tool, but\par no more after that. \par     Against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the dollar rose\par 0.068% to 102.57, after slipping 0.24% overnight. The dollar\par index is on course to log a decline of about 1.5% for the month.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rodrigo Catril\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 National\par Australia Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said U.S. data was feeding the theme of\par "sectoral recessions" occurring with different lags, making the\par Fed's job of taming inflation harder. \par     "Overall, the data is telling us the Fed needs to keep its\par foot on the tightening pedal," he said.\par     Investor attention will firmly be on Fed Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome\par Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2 's comments at the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Forum in Sintra,\par Portugal. \par     Powell will participate in a panel later on Wednesday\par alongside \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  Governor Andrew Bailey, \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christine Lagarde\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par Governor Kazuo Ueda.\par     After spiking 0.5% higher on Tuesday, the euro\par eased 0.09% to $1.0949. Sterling last fetched $1.2729,\par down 0.13% on the day.\par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0444 GMT\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct     High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                 \par                                               Session                                           \par  Euro/Dollar                  $1.0949        $1.0962     -0.11%         +2.19%      +1.0962     +1.0942\par  Dollar/Yen                   143.9550       144.0650    -0.09%         +9.67%      +144.0400   +143.7500\par  Euro/Yen         <EURJPY=EB  157.63         157.90      -0.17%         +12.35%     +157.9200   +157.4400\par                   S>                                                                            \par  Dollar/Swiss                 0.8941         0.8936      +0.08%         -3.28%      +0.8948     +0.8933\par  Sterling/Dollar              1.2728         1.2748      -0.12%         +5.28%      +1.2751     +1.2726\par  Dollar/Canadian              1.3214         1.3192      +0.17%         -2.47%      +1.3215     +1.3190\par  Aussie/Dollar                0.6643         0.6686      -0.64%         -2.55%      +0.6689     +0.6618\par  NZ                           0.6117         0.6163      -0.73%         -3.65%      +0.6165     +0.6114\par  Dollar/Dollar                                                                                  \par                                                                                                 \par     \par All spots\par Tokyo spots\par Europe spots \par Volatilities \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par \par     \par  (Reporting by Ankur Banerjee in Singapore; Editing by\par