\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-FACTBOX-Japan's toolkit to combat sharp yen declines\b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2023\par 01:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats item that ran June 27 with no change to text)\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 27 (Reuters) - Japanese authorities are facing renewed pressure to combat the yen's fresh declines driven by market expectations that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will keep interest rates ultra-low, even as other central banks tighten monetary policy to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 Here are possible steps the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take to tackle further yen weakness, which gives exports a boost but hurts households and retailers by inflating already rising import costs for fuel and food.\par \par \uc2 ESCALATE VERBAL \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  - HIGHLY LIKELY\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities began jawboning markets this week, describing recent yen falls as "sharp and one-sided". Top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Masato Kanda also said he would not rule out any options, when asked if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could become a possibility.\par \par \uc2 If the pace of yen declines accelerates, authorities may escalate their warnings to promise "decisive action" against speculative moves.\par \par \uc2 Such remarks, aired prior to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, would signal that Tokyo was edging closer to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 CONDUCT YEN-BUYING \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  - LESS LIKELY\par \par \uc2 Tokyo made rare forays into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the yen in September and October last year to stem a plunge in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that eventually hit a 32-year low of 151.94 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 While the yen is still well off that low, many market players see 145 as Tokyo's line-in-the-sand which, if breached, could trigger another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar/yen stood around 143.60 in Asia on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Authorities have said the speed of yen moves, rather than levels, were key to deciding whether to step into the market. This means the chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will rise if the yen's declines are rapid and viewed as driven mostly by speculative trading.\par \par \uc2 But yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be costly as authorities must tap \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves for dollars to sell.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo would also need consent from other major economies, particularly the United States, to ensure the scale of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is sufficient to turn the tide.\par \par \uc2 BOJ\uc2  RAISES INTEREST RATES - HIGHLY UNLIKELY\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) has vowed to keep interest rates ultra-low to support the economy, even as inflation exceeded its 2% target for more than a year.\par \par \uc2 The dovish stance is partly driving the yen's fall, as markets focus on the divergence between Japan and U.S. and European central banks, which have hiked rates aggressively.\par \par \uc2 Some market players speculate the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  may allow interest rates to rise, such as by raising an implicit 0.5% cap on its 10-year bond yield target, as early as July.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 BOJ\uc2  policymakers are cautious of taking such steps too soon, given uncertainty on whether wages will keep rising, and the risk of a deeper global economic slump hitting Japan's fragile, export-reliant recovery.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  also has no intention of using monetary policy tools to directly curb yen declines - a move that could be interpreted as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation and would go beyond its remit.\par \par \uc2 That means the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  will consider tweaking its yield control policy only if inflation rises for longer than expected, and prods firms to raise wages and prices on a sustained basis. (Reporting by Leika Kihara; Additional reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Clarence Fernandez)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-30T23:17:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230627ej6r03mmt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
