\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar hits 7-month high against yen; \uc2 ECB\uc2  comments boost euro\b0\par\par\uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2023\par 14:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Harry Robertson and Rocky Swift\par \par \uc2 LONDON/TOKYO, June 27 (Reuters) - The dollar rose to a seven-month high against the yen on Tuesday before paring its gains, with investors on the look-out for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the euro picked up against the dollar as investors listened closely to policymakers' speeches at the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual forum at Sintra in Portugal.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to 143.94 yen, its highest since Nov. 10, despite Japanese officials vowing to respond appropriately if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves became excessive. It was last up 0.1% at 143.63 yen to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said on Tuesday: "We will closely watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves with a strong sense of urgency and will respond appropriately if the moves become excessive."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the yen last year when it weakened past the 145 per dollar level. It has recently fallen sharply as U.S. interest rates have soared above those in Japan, making U.S. bonds look more attractive.\par \par \uc2 Many investors and analysts believe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a possibility after the government stepped up its comments on the situation in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 "If big data comes out of the U.S. in the next couple of weeks (and) dollar-yen spikes above 145, then I would think that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  would step in, or threaten to step in," \uc2 Francesco Pesole\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ING, said.\par \par \uc2 The euro was last up 0.37% against the dollar at $1.095, after rising slightly on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Euro-dollar is a bit stronger this morning, we had probably a bit of help from hawkish \uc2 ECB\uc2  (\uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) comments this morning," said ING's Pesole.\par \par \uc2 Latvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor and \uc2 ECB\uc2  official \uc2 Martins Kazaks\uc2  said in Portugal on Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely keep hiking interest rates after July.\par \par \uc2 The euro zone's key interest rate currently stands at 3.5%. Kazaks' comments suggest they could go to 4% or higher.\par \par \uc2 ECB\uc2  President \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  also spoke in Sintra on Tuesday, saying that "policy needs to be decided meeting by meeting and has to remain data-dependent".\par \par \uc2 The dollar index was 0.19% lower at 102.55, weighed down by the euro, which is its biggest component.\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  governor Andrew Bailey, and \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  Governor Kazuo Ueda are due to speak at a panel with Lagarde on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Investors also had U.S. data to look forward to, with durable goods orders and building permits figures due later on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the Russian rouble weakened 0.93% versus the dollar to 85.19. It hit its weakest level since March 2022 on Monday at 87 roubles to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  said on Monday he let an aborted mutiny go on as long as it did to avoid bloodshed. On Tuesday, Russia's security service dropped its criminal case against the Wagner mercenary group over the brief rebellion.\par \par \uc2 Sterling was last trading at $1.272, up less than 0.1% on the day.\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell 0.36% against the offshore Chinese yuan to 7.217 on Tuesday, after hitting a 7-month high of 7.243 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Investors braced for the possibility of more support measures after China returned from a holiday on Monday. \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its daily yuan fixing stronger than market expectations for a second day in a row on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Sources said state-owned banks had been selling dollars in the offshore spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, increasing speculation authorities were becoming less tolerant of yuan weakness.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Harry Robertson in London and Rocky Swift in Tokyo; Editing by Barbara Lewis, Conor Humphries and Chizu Nomiyama) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-27T13:07:48.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230627ej6r01sl2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
