\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Japan's financial authorities warn of "rapid" yen depreciation\b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The new depreciation of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is blamed on the continued distancing between U.S. monetary policies.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Vice Finance Minister Masato Kanda said Monday that the yen's depreciation against the U.S. dollar is "rapid and one-sided," raising alarms after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate fell to the 143 yen range today.\par \par \uc2 "It is desirable for a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to develop, however, a rapid and one-sided movement is appreciated, therefore, we will watch carefully and take action if an extraordinary movement is seen," Kanda told the media today.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the possibility of Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the vice minister said that "no option is ruled out."\par \par \uc2 During the first half hour of trading in Tokyo, the yen moved today between 143.26 and 143.71 yen per dollar, approaching the psychological barrier of 145 yen and raising alarms among analysts about a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Executive to stop the fall of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  already made \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September and October last year in an attempt to halt the sharp fall of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the US dollar, but has not taken additional measures since then.\par \par \uc2 The further depreciation of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being blamed on the continued drift between the monetary policies of the US and major European central banks - which are opting for aggressive rate hikes - and that of the \uc2 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is continuing with its ultra-low rate strategy.\par \par \uc2 The weakness of the yen, at the same time, is favorable for major Japanese exporters, which has led to increased optimism on the \uc2 Tokyo Stock Exchange\uc2 , which is on a winning streak that has taken its benchmark index, the Nikkei, to levels not seen since 1990, in the midst of the financial bubble.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230626ej6q009zr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
