\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Japan's top  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  diplomat escalates warning against weak yen\b0\par\par\uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2023\par 10:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par         * \par       Yen at 7-mth low vs dollar, 15-yr trough to euro\par     \par \par         * \par       Divergence of monetary policy boosts dlr, weaken yen\par     \par \par         * \par       \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in October to stem yen weakness\par     \par \par         * \par       Investors brace for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if yen falls to 145\par     \par \par   \par  (Updates with government spokesman comment, detail)\par     By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par        TOKYO, June 26 (Reuters) - Japan is not ruling out any\par options in responding appropriately to excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves,\par its top \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  diplomat said on Monday, stepping up warnings\par against recent yen weakening that was "rapid and one-sided".\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should move in a stable way, reflecting\par fundamentals, the government said, after the yen weakened beyond\par 143 yen        on Friday, a seven-month low versus the dollar,\par and fell to a 15-year low beyond 155 yen to the euro.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , often perceived as a safe-haven asset, is\par coming under renewed selling pressure, threatening consumers\par with an import cost spike.\par     "We have all options available and we are not ruling out\par any," Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Masato\par Kanda told reporters when asked whether authorities stood ready\par to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market. \par     "I won't comment on what to do now."\par     A monetary policy divergence between the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\par and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  was seen as driving up the dollar,\par as Japan continues easing while the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par tightened policy aggressively to fight inflation.\par     The government was closely monitoring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market,\par its top spokesperson said.\par     "It's important for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to move stably\par reflecting fundamentals," Chief Cabinet Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hirokazu\par Matsuno\f28 \uc2 \f2  told reporters. "The government will closely watch the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market with a strong sense of urgency and respond\par appropriately to excessive moves."\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last conducted rare yen-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in October\par to stem weakening after it plunged to a 32-year low of near 152\par yen to the dollar.\par     "The dollar was trading around 145 yen when Japanese\par authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last September, so market players put a \par threshold beyond 145 yen as a red zone," said Daisaku Ueno,\par chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "Chances of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will grow if authorities escalate\par warnings to say things like they are 'deeply concerned' and/or\par 'ready to take decisive action'."\par     Kanda, asked about the chances of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said he\par would not rule any option out.\par     "Regardless of the direction, it's generally not good for\par Japan's economy and global economy if exchange rates move\par excessively in a way that deviates from economic fundamentals,"\par Kanda said.\par     "Underlying moves are rapid and one-sided."\par     Authorities were focusing on the pace of moves in the yen,\par rather than its levels, he said.\par     Investors have been selling yen after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  kept interest\par rates ultra-low at a two-day policy review ending on June 16,\par when it vowed to maintain its stimulus, in contrast with other\par central banks tightening policy to ease stubborn inflation.\par \par  (Writing by Leika Kihara and Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Kim\par Coghill and Jamie Freed)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-26T09:19:07.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230625ej6p00xy9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
