\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Oil up, stocks dip after short-lived Russian mutiny\b0\par\par\uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2023\par 02:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, June 26 (Reuters) - Stocks slipped slightly and oil rose in early trade on Monday as investors figured an abortive weekend mutiny by Russian mercenaries raised questions about stability and crude supply.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude futures rose 1% to $74.55 a barrel and U.S. crude poked above $70, recouping a little of losses made last week. Japan's Nikkei fell 0.2% and Australia's ASX 200 fell 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 The safe-haven yen also rose a bit, though it had help from hints at possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat and a summary of opinions showing a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member pushed for a debate on its yield curve control policy.\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 futures were 0.2% higher.\par \par \uc2 Russian mercenaries made a short-lived rebellion on Saturday, seizing the southern city of Rostov and advancing on Moscow demanding the removal of Russian military commanders in charge of the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The private Wagner army then withdrew after striking a deal guaranteeing their safety and the exile of their leader, \uc2 Yevgeny Prigozhin\uc2 , to Belarus. The consequences for the Ukraine war were not clear, though the challenge to Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's authority was the starkest in decades of his leadership.\par \par \uc2 "Geopolitical risk amid internal instability in Russia has increased," said \uc2 Rystad Energy\uc2  analysts Jorge Leon. "As such, we are likely to see a marginal uptick in oil prices in the coming days, if the situation does not deteriorate."\par \par \uc2 U.S. Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  said the turmoil in Russia could take months to play out, while Italy's foreign minister said it had shattered the "myth" of Russian unity.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere markets were already on edge about a darkening growth outlook, as China's post-pandemic recovery stalls and global interest rates remain high, and traders were unwilling to take any new positions on the basis of Russian events.\par \par \uc2 The risk-sensitive Australian dollar was steady at $0.6679. The euro nursed last week's modest drop at $1.0906 and sterling held at $1.2728.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think the market can get its head around working out if there are implications," said \uc2 Ray Attrill\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2  in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 "People may think that ultimately Putin's grip on power is weakened here. Maybe the Ukrainians may be emboldened to be upping their counteroffensives," he said, but without obvious progress traders in Asia would be focused on China.\par \par \uc2 China returns from holidays with the yuan having dropped sharply in offshore trade, leaving investors looking to the morning's fix of the onshore trading band for signs of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's level of comfort with the slide.\par \par \uc2 The offshore yuan last traded at 7.21 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen, which has been on a slide as global interest rate expectations rise and Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stays steadfastly dovish, bounced about 0.3% to 143.31 per dollar\par \par \uc2 Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Masato Kanda said on Monday authorities will respond to any excessive moves and did not rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as happened last year. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should also discuss revising its yield curve control policy at an early stage, a board member was quoted as saying at a June policy meeting, a summary of opinions released on Monday showed.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Stephen Coates) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-26T01:46:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230626ej6q002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
