\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Japan redoubles its vigilance on the yen: the fall is going too far\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Japan is monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the face of the recent acceleration of the yen's depreciation, Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said Tuesday, after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a seven-month low against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The greenback today surpassed 142 yen or 0.0076 dollars per Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  unit, accelerating its recent pace of depreciation against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in the face of continued divergent monetary policies between the two countries and rising interest rates in Europe, which has placed the euro at its highest level with the yen in 15 years, the 155 units.\par \par \uc2 "Exchange rates are determined by markets and other factors, but they should remain stable," Suzuki said during a press conference reported by the local news agency Kyodo. The Japanese finance minister added that this is "the basic stance" of the Japanese government.\par \par \uc2 Suzuki also stressed that they are constantly monitoring developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. After Japan was removed from the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch list, the minister assured that Tokyo will maintain close communication with other countries and take "necessary" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures. The yen hit a 1998 low several months ago, and although it has recovered slightly, it is still at very low levels.\par \par \uc2 The recent depreciation of the yen against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has accelerated since the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BoJ) decided last week to maintain its ultra-loose monetary policy, with negative benchmark interest rates of -0.1%.\par \par \uc2 This decision contrasts with the stance of the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  (Fed), which, while maintaining rates in June, has signaled its intention to raise them further in the future. For its part, the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ) continued with its rate hikes and raised interest rates by a quarter point to 4%.\par \par \uc2 The divergence between the monetary policies of the most influential central banks already led to a depreciation of the yen last year, which prompted the Japanese government to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on several occasions to halt the accelerated fall of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yen's weakness has had an impact on import costs in Japan, a country highly dependent on these purchases, which has led to higher prices for the population on a day-to-day basis.\par \par \uc2 Despite past \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  (the first time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought yen since 1998 and the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sale conducted by the Japanese government following the yen's surge after the Fukushima accident), Washington has removed Japan from its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch list after eight years.\par \par \uc2 Suzuki explained that this decision is the result of close communication between the two countries' authorities and stated that Japan's removal from the list "will not change or affect" Japan's stance on these policies.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230620ej6k0064h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
