\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-GRAPHIC-Take Five: Almost half-time\b0\par\par\uc2 852 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2023\par 08:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats Friday story to include OPEC+ decision)\par \par \uc2 June 2 (Reuters) - The hefty weight of tech megacaps, a suspense-packed \uc2 OPEC\uc2  meeting at the weekend and more pain for consumers and businesses Down Under - these are just some of the topics preoccupying markets as they approach the halfway point of 2023.\par \par \uc2 Here's a look at the week ahead in markets from Kevin Buckland in Tokyo; Ira Iosebashvili in New York and Dhara Ranasinghe, Karin Strohecker and Amanda Cooper in London.\par \par \uc2 1/THE NARROWEST RALLY THIS CENTURY\par \par \uc2 Some investors are growing concerned about how gains in the S&P 500 have become increasingly concentrated in a handful of megacap stocks.\par \par \uc2 The combined weight of five stocks - \uc2 Apple\uc2 , \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , \uc2 Google\uc2 -parent \uc2 Alphabet\uc2 , \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and \uc2 Nvidia\uc2  - now accounts for 25% of the S&P 500\u8217\'20\'19s market value, a trend recently supercharged by the AI buzz. Data from \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  shows the equal-weighted S&P 500 index, a barometer of the average stock, trailing the S&P 500 by its biggest margin since 1999.\par \par \uc2 A rally driven by a handful of stocks raises questions about the health of the broader market and risks igniting volatility if investors ditch those megacap holdings.\par \par \uc2 2/FIRST IN, FIRST OUT\par \par \uc2 Emerging market central banks were quick to tighten policy in early 2021 when price pressures accelerated, front-running major developed central banks, including the Fed. Now they appear to be once again first out of the starting blocks as rate cuts move higher up the agenda.\par \par \uc2 Hungary became the first European bank to lower rates in May, following Uruguay, which kicked off the Latin American rate-cut cycle in April while Sri Lanka stunned markets with a 250-basis point rate cut on June 1.\par \par \uc2 But the picture is mixed: Polish policymakers are seen holding rates at 6.75% on Tuesday even if expectations are rising for a cut later in the year. Markets might have to wait until 2024 for India, where the next decision is due on Thursday. Russia is expected to keep its rate at 7.5% on Friday.\par \par \uc2 3/A CRUDE INVITATION\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  and partners agreed on Sunday to extend a set of production cuts into 2024. The event draws in throngs of reporters from all around the world, who jostle for position at the bottom of several flights of stairs at the \uc2 OPEC\uc2  secretariat that they race up to get into the pre-meeting press scrum.\par \par \uc2 Reading the runes was already tricky and Saudi Arabia, the group's biggest exporter, unexpectedly delivered a deep cut to its own output. Saudi Energy Minister \uc2 Prince Abdulaziz\uc2  told a news conference the reduction was "a Saudi lollipop". "We wanted to ice the cake. We always want to add suspense," he said.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the suspense in the run-up to the weekend, the group banned several major news organisations from attending the press conference,\par \par \uc2 including Reuters and \uc2 Bloomberg\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The price of oil rose as much as 3.4% overnight to a high of $78.73 a barrel. But despite OPEC+'s best efforts, it's still worth roughly half what it was in March 2022, after Russia invaded Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 4/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WATCH\par \par \uc2 The yen has fallen over 5% since early March to six-month lows against a resilient dollar.\par \par \uc2 It's enough to make Japanese officials uneasy, with top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Masato Kanda warning that Japan will closely watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves and won't rule out any options.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is viewed as a distant prospect, but traders will likely pay attention to policymaker comments in coming days after officials from the finance ministry, \uc2 BOJ\uc2  and Japan's financial watchdog met on Tuesday. Such meetings can be a prelude to further action.\par \par \uc2 And it's not just \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch. Sweden's crown is at its weakest against the dollar and euro in over a decade, adding to inflationary pressures. A weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a problem, but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a last resort, says \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Per Jansson.\par \par \uc2 Such resolve could well be put to the test.\par \par \uc2 5/\uc2 RBA\uc2  BRINGS THE PAIN\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  says the inflation fight is far from won, and the public should brace itself for more pain.\par \par \uc2 That could be as soon as the next meeting on Tuesday, with markets laying about 30% odds for a hike.\par \par \uc2 The economy had been showing signs of cooling until this week, when a reading of consumer prices jumped much more than forecast for April, sending stocks to a two-month trough.\par \par \uc2 Rates are already at an 11-year peak after a surprise hike last month, which \uc2 RBA\uc2  governor \uc2 Philip Lowe\uc2  justified by saying he wanted to send a clear message to households and businesses that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do whatever it takes.\par \par \uc2 Policymakers need to keep an eye on top trading partner China too, where a sputtering post-pandemic recovery risks eroding Australian ore and energy exports.\par \par \uc2 (Compiled by Amanda Cooper; Editing by Edwina Gibbs) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-6-5T07:23:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230605ej6500pru\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
