 firm whose report, dated April 26, 2019, expressed an unqualified opinion on those financial highlights.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8203\'20\'0B \u8203\'20\'0B\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Basis for Opinion\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8203\'20\'0B \u8203\'20\'0B\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 These financial statements are the responsibility of the Fund's management. Our responsibility is to express an opinion on the Fund's financial statements based on our audits. We are a public accounting firm registered with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Public Company Accounting Oversight Board\f28 \uc2 \f2  (United States) ("PCAOB") and are required to be independent with respect to the Fund in accordance with the U.S. federal securities laws and the applicable rules and regulations of the Securities and Exchange Commission and the PCAOB.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8203\'20\'0B \u8203\'20\'0B\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We conducted our audits in accordance with the standards of the PCAOB. Those standards require that we plan and perform the audit to obtain reasonable assurance about whether the financial statements are free of material misstatement, whether due to error or fraud. The Fund is not required to have, nor were we engaged to perform, an audit of the Fund's internal control over financial reporting. As part of our audits we are required to obtain an understanding of internal control over financial reporting but not for the purpose of expressing an opinion on the effectiveness of the Fund's internal control over financial reporting. Accordingly, we express no such opinion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8203\'20\'0B \u8203\'20\'0B\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our audits included performing procedures to assess the risks of material misstatement of the financial statements, whether due to error or fraud, and performing procedures that respond to those risks. Such procedures included examining, on a test basis, evidence regarding the amounts and disclosures in the financial statements. Our procedures included confirmation of securities owned as of February 28, 2023, by correspondence with the custodian and brokers. Our audits also included evaluating the accounting principles used and significant estimates made by management, as well as evaluating the overall presentation of the financial statements. We believe that our audits provide a reasonable basis for our opinion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8203\'20\'0B \u8203\'20\'0B\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8203\'20\'0B \u8203\'20\'0B\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We have served as the auditor of one or more Nomura investment companies since 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8203\'20\'0B \u8203\'20\'0B\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New York, New York\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 April 27, 2023\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u8203\'20\'0B\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAPAN SMALLER CAPITALIZATION FUND, INC\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SCHEDULE OF INVESTMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FEBRUARY 28, 2023\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                         \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B  Shares     \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B  Fair Value\par JAPANESE EQUITY SECURITIES              \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B             \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B   \par                                         \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B             \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B   \par Banks - 7.9%                            \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B             \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B   \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Daishi Hokuetsu Financial Group, Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .   \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B  66,900     \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B  $1,597,715\par Okinawa Financial Group, Inc.           \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B  158,900    \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B  2,789,522\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Akita Bank, Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .                    \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B  267,400    \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B  3,892,563\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Saga Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .                   \u8203\'20\'0B   \u8203\'20\'0B  61,300     \u8