---------------- \par  NAV per Ordinary Share               140.46p            137.90p \par --------------------------  -----------------  ----------------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 14. RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transactions with the Investment Adviser\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The fees for the year are disclosed in note 5 and amounts outstanding at the year ended 31 December 2022 were GBP nil.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A key member of the RSM team is a major shareholder of Rosenwald Capital Management, Inc.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rosenwald Capital Management Inc, receives dividends paid by the Company based on its shareholding.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Directors' fees and shareholdings\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Directors' fees are payable at the rate of GBP27,810 per annum for each Director other than the Chairman, who is entitled to receive GBP41,000. The Chairman of the Audit Committee is also entitled to an additional fee of GBP5,190 per annum.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Directors had the following shareholdings in the Company, all of which were beneficially owned. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                   As at         As at \par                             31 December   31 December \par                                    2022          2021 \par ------------------  -------------------  ------------ \par   Rosemary Morgan                40,000        40,000 \par ------------------  -------------------  ------------ \par   Chetan Ghosh                   40,000        40,000 \par ------------------  -------------------  ------------ \par   Rachel Hill                   115,791       115,791 \par ------------------  -------------------  ------------ \par   Alicia Ogawa                   25,000        25,000 \par ------------------  -------------------  ------------ \par   Ayako Weissman                 27,000        27,000 \par ------------------  -------------------  ------------ \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 15. FINANCIAL INSTRUMENTS AND CAPITAL DISCLOSURES\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risk Management Policies and Procedures\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As an investment trust the Company invests in equities for the long term in order to achieve its investment objective. In pursuing its investment objective, the Company is exposed to a variety of risks that could result in either a reduction in the Company's net assets or a reduction of the profits available for dividends.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 These risks include market risk (comprising \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk, interest rate risk, and other price risk), liquidity risk, credit risk and the Directors' approach to the management of them are set out follows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The objectives, policies and processes for managing the risks and the methods used to measure the risks, are set out below.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Market risk\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economic conditions\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Changes in economic conditions in Japan (for example, interest rates and rates of inflation, industry conditions, competition, political and diplomatic events and other factors) and in the countries in which the Company's investee companies operate could substantially and adversely affect the Company's prospects.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sectoral diversification\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company is not subject to restrictions on the amount it may invest in any particular sector. Although the portfolio is expected to be diversified in terms of sector exposures, the Company may have significant exposure to portfolio companies from certain sectors from time to time. As there is no hard limit on the amount the Company may invest in any sector the entire Portfolio may, at certain times, be invested solely in one sector. Greater concentration of investments in any one sector may result in greater volatility in the value of the Company's investments and consequently its NAV and may materially and adversely affect the performance of the Company and returns to Shareholders.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Management of market risks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company is invested in a diversified portfolio of investments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Board will not set any limits on sector weightings or stock selection within the portfolio. The Board will apply the following restrictions on the size of its investments:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- not more than 30 per cent. of the Gross Asset Value at the time of investment will be invested in the securities of a single issuer; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- the value of the four largest investments at the time of investment will not constitute more than 75 per cent. of the Gross Asset Value.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (a) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The majority of the Company's assets will be denominated in a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  other than sterling (predominantly in Japanese yen) and changes in the exchange rate between sterling and Japanese yen may lead to a depreciation of the value of the Company's assets as expressed in sterling and may reduce the returns to the Company from its investments and, therefore, negatively impact the level of dividends paid to Shareholders.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Management of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company does not currently intend to enter into any arrangements to hedge its underlying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exposure to investment denominated in Japanese yen, although the Investment Adviser and the Board may review this from time to time.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exposures\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An analysis of the Company's equity investments that are priced in a foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                                              As at 31 December  As at 31 December \par                                                           2022               2021 \par                                                        GBP'000            GBP'000 \par -----------------------------------  -------------------------  ----------------- \par   Portfolio of investments: yen                        126,284            138,626 \par -----------------------------------  -------------------------  ----------------- \par   Trade and other receivables: yen                         985              1,625 \par -----------------------------------  -------------------------  ----------------- \par   Cash: yen                                             31,762             15,131 \par -----------------------------------  -------------------------  ----------------- \par   Total                                                159,031            155,382 \par -----------------------------------  -------------------------  ----------------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sensitivity\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If the Japanese yen had appreciated or depreciated by 10% as at 31 December 2022 then the value of the portfolio as at that date would have increased or decreased as shown below. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Increase     Decrease     Increase     Decrease \par          in           in           in           in \par  Fair Value   Fair Value   Fair Value   Fair Value \par              -----------  -----------  ----------- \par       As at        As at        As at        As at \par              -----------  -----------  ----------- \par 31 December  31 December  31 December  31 December \par              -----------  -----------  ----------- \par        2022         2022         2021         2021 \par              -----------  -----------  ----------- \par     GBP'000      GBP'000      GBP'000      GBP'000 \par              -----------  -----------  ----------- \par  \par  \par  Impact on portfolio - increase/(decrease)              12,628  (12,628)  13,863 (13,863) \par -------------------------------------------  -----------------  --------  --------------- \par  Impact on NAV - increase/(decrease)                    15,903  (15,903)  15,538 (15,538) \par -------------------------------------------  -----------------  --------  --------------- \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (b) Interest rate risks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company is exposed to interest rate risk specifically through its cash holdings. Interest rate movements may affect the level of income receivable from any cash on deposit with banks. The effect of interest rate changes on the earnings of the companies held within the portfolio may have a significant impact on the valuation of the Company's investments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Management of interest rate risks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prevailing interest rates are taken into account when deciding on borrowings.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interest rate exposure\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 06-04-23 0600GMT\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RNS0000020230406ej460002u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
