m 3.79% pre \uc2 RBA\uc2  statement \u8226\'20\'22 Powell speech tonight likely pivotal for the USD after huge U.S. payrolls \u8226\'20\'22 Charts; momentum studies slide, 5, 10 & 21 DMAs crest or fall \u8226\'20\'22 21 day Bollinger bands flat line - recent fall leaves a negative setup \u8226\'20\'22 Resistance starts 0.6987, 5 DMA and 0.6997 21 DMA next significant levels\par \par \uc2 GBP/USD-Gently bid with risk appetite and better data\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 +0.25% in a 1.2018-1.2057 range with only modest interest on D3 \u8226\'20\'22 Resilient UK demand for films and holidays as confidence rises \u8226\'20\'22 Mild UK winter halved the expected cost of UK energy support schemes NAO \u8226\'20\'22 Data suggests that dire predictions for cost of living perhaps overdone \u8226\'20\'22 Techs; 5, 10 & 21 day moving averages head lower, 21 day Bolli bands expand \u8226\'20\'22 Momentum studies slide - dip leaves a bearish setup on daily charts \u8226\'20\'22 1.1984, 76.4% of the 2023 rise is first support, then the 1.1842 2023 base \u8226\'20\'22 1.2077 NY high then 1.2143 5 DMA are initial resistance\par \par \uc2 RBI\uc2  to hike rates 25bps on Wed, dovish guidance likely\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  is likely to raise its key repo rate by 25 basis points to 6.5% on Wednesday and hint that it is nearing the end of its tightening cycle. While December retail inflation edged lower to 5.72%, remaining within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tolerance zone of 2%-6% for a second consecutive month, core CPI remained sticky at an estimated 6.1%. The Indian government has just delivered a fiscally prudent budget and central banks globally are moving towards a pause on rate rises. The government expects economic growth of 6% to 6.8% in the 2023/24 fiscal year beginning in April, slowing from a projected 7% in the current year. These are all compelling reasons for the \uc2 RBI\uc2  to opt for a smaller quarter-point hike and signal a move to a neutral policy stance. Indeed, 40 of 52 economists in a Reuters poll forecast a 25 bps hike on Wednesday; the remaining 12 predicted no change. The median forecast was for rates to remain at 6.50% until the end of 2023. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation forecast and management of the government's borrowing programme will be scrutinised, while Governor \uc2 Shaktikanta Das\uc2  might also face questions on the banking sector's exposure to the embattled \uc2 Adani Group\uc2 . USD/INR is likely to consolidate in a broad 81.00-83.50 range and the current rally will face strong resistance at 83.00-05 and 83.25-30.XX\par \par \uc2 To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-2-10T05:42:02.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230207ej2700uh9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
