\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  confirms record  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  to support yen\b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2023\par 03:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds finance minister, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data, detail)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed on Tuesday that it made record \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in October, selling the dollar worth 6.35 trillion yen ($48 billion) to support the yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) data showed.\par \par \uc2 The quarterly data showed a steep drop in the yen to a 32-year low of 151.94 to the dollar on Oct. 21 triggered the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that day, followed by another on Oct. 24.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were aimed at countering excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves driven by speculative trading, and they had certain effects," Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  told reporters. "We'll continue to monitor market moves carefully."\par \par \uc2 Suzuki said it was important for \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move stably reflecting economic fundamentals, and that future \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not entirely ruled out.\par \par \uc2 The stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or making a foray in the market without announcing it, came after Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the yen for dollars for the first time in 24 years on Sept. 22.\par \par \uc2 Japan spent a record 5.62 trillion yen ($42.5 billion) on a single day yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Oct. 21 and further 730 billion yen on Oct. 24, having spent 2.84 trillion yen on Sept. 22 to stem the yen's sharp fall, which boosted living costs for resource-deficiant Japan.\par \par \uc2 The dollar has pulled back to move in a range around 130 yen since then, while stoking some concerns about renewed yen rises, which could hamper Japanese exports of cars and electronics.\par \par \uc2 It was rare for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to conduct yen-buying, dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the country's past battle with a strong yen making Japanese goods less competitive overseas.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  publishes monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  records at the end of each month, and it issues daily results for the prior quarter.\par \par \uc2 Separate MOF data on Tuesday showed Japan's foreign reserves rose for the third straight month to $1.25 trillion at the end of January, boosted by interest payments on foreign bonds, waning interest rates, softening of dollar and gains in gold.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 132.3600 yen) (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Stephen Coates) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-2-7T03:45:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230207ej2700gqt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
