\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 IMF\uc2  leaves message to future BoJ Governor: "clarity" and "flexibility" in controlling yieds\b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) has warned that an abrupt change in monetary policy by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BoJ) could have a "contagion effect" on the financial market, so the institution should clearly define the path to adopt in the future.\par \par \uc2 IMF\uc2  Deputy Director Gina Gopinath, quoted by the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2 , called on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adopt a flexible approach to controlling debt yields, given the risks of high inflation in the short term\par \par \uc2 . In December, Japan's consumer price index reached four-decade highs. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has resisted adopting a tight monetary policy, opting instead to maintain an accommodative policy.\par \par \uc2 Read Also \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the second time in two months Still, "we believe it is important that [the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] maintain an accommodative monetary policy," Gopinath stressed.\par \par \uc2 "Y\par \par \uc2 ieldcurve control is one part of this toolkit," he added, explaining that "we see a significant risk of high inflation," so "increasing flexibility [in controlling the curve] is a help\par \par \uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Gopinath also acknowledged that the Japanese economy is going through a "delicate environment." The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will change governors in April, at a time when the market is pushing for the institution to ditch the "doves" and turn to "hawks."\par \par \uc2 Read Also Read Major Japanese banks suspend transactions with Russian \uc2 Sberbank\uc2  At the last monetary policy meeting, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  led by \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  resisted this pressure and kept key interest rates unchanged, as well as the range set in December - which serves as the limit for ten-year debt "yields" - between -0.5% and 0.5%\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230126ej1q0070o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
