\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Japan's top  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  diplomat warns sharp  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  moves won't be tolerated\b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2023\par 05:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to attach to alerts)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 26 (Reuters) -\par \par \uc2 Sharp one-sided \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves cannot be tolerated, Japan's top finance diplomat Masato Kanda told Reuters, reaffirming Tokyo's determination to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb any speculative or significant yen moves.\par \par \uc2 "Sharp, one-sided moves as seen last year are not desirable or cannot be tolerated from the viewpoints of the people's livelihood and corporate activity," Kanda said on Wednesday, referring to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 24 years last year.\par \par \uc2 Kanda oversaw \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted last year to prop up the yen after it fell around 30% to 32-year lows near 152 to the dollar. The yen has rebounded since then and it is now trading around 130 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "There's no change to this thinking from now on as well," Kanda, who is vice finance minister for international affairs, said in an interview, when asked whether sharp yen rises warrant action.\par \par \uc2 Kanda emphasised that the government aims to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves stable, while the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) has independence in guiding monetary policy and focuses on achieving price stability.\par \par \uc2 "Generally speaking, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  targets price stability, while we aim for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We are communicating firmly with the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  as well as other central banks. But policy itself is independent," Kanda said of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's ultra-loose monetary policy has drawn criticism from some analysts as having triggered an unwelcome yen plunge last year that inflated the cost of raw material imports.\par \par \uc2 Separately, Tokyo plans to spearhead discussions on ramping up a regional multilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps arrangement called Chiang-Mai Initiative Multilateralisation (CMIM), to prepare against future financial crises and natural disasters, Kanda said. (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Additional reporting by Kentaro Sugiyama Editing by Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-1-26T05:13:08.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230126ej1q00d71\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
