\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Japan foreign reserves rise to highest in six years\b0\par\par\uc2 425 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2022\par 03:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves up for first time in 4 months\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tokyo conducted no \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Nov as yen rebounded\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Softer dollar boosts euro and other foreign assets\par \par \uc2 (Adds context on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trends)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 7 (Reuters) - Japan's foreign reserves rose in November to their highest in six years, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday, as the dollar's retreat boosted the value of non-dollar foreign assets and authorities refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves grew 2.65% from the previous month to $1.226 trillion at the end of November, the first rise in four months and their highest since December 2016, ministry officials said.\par \par \uc2 Investors are scrutinising \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  records for clues on how much \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be able to spend to stem yen weakness, although the recent reversal of dollar strength has eased pressure on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar has fallen about 10% against the yen since hitting a 32-year high of almost 152 yen in October. The dollar pulled back as speculation mounted that the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's aggressive interest rate hikes may be peaking out and inflation may be nearing a ceiling.\par \par \uc2 Japan's foreign reserves were whittled down in September and October by the authorities' dollar-selling and yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when they sought to rein in the yen's sharp decline against the dollar. A rise in foreign bond yields also trimmed the value of the reserves.\par \par \uc2 With those factors no longer in play, other factors that boost reserves - interest earned on foreign bond holdings, declines in overseas yields, appreciation of the euro against the dollar, and higher gold prices - drove up Japan's foreign reserves in November, the ministry officials said.\par \par \uc2 Foreign bonds, most of which are widely believed to be U.S. Treasuries bought during bouts of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the yen was strong, account for about four-fifths of Japan's reserves.\par \par \uc2 Deposits, mostly parked at overseas central banks and the \uc2 Bank for International Settlements\uc2 , make up about one-tenth of the reserves, while gold accounts for about 4%.\par \par \uc2 Japan spent a record 6.35 trillion yen ($46.28 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October, adding to 2.8 trillion yen spent on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September. The authorities did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, in November. ($1 = 137.2000 yen) (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Edmund Klamann) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-12-7T03:25:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221207eic7005k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
